WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.935
Welcome to the Accelerometer Learning
Course. In Module 1, we

00:00:04.935 --> 00:00:07.200
start at the very beginning,

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.790
with a question that sounds simple but
shapes everything that

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:12.320
follows. What, exactly, is

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:15.760
an accelerometer? Let's find out.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:19.342
At its core, an accelerometer is a sensor
that records

00:00:19.342 --> 00:00:21.200
acceleration over time. Most

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.961
research-grade devices measure this along
three axes,

00:00:23.961 --> 00:00:25.940
capturing movement in three dimensions

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:30.405
as the body moves. On its own, the device
simply produces a

00:00:30.405 --> 00:00:32.600
continuous stream of numbers.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:36.440
It does not label what that movement
means.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:39.200
Here is the key idea for this whole
course. The accelerometer

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.240
does not know whether a

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.800
person is exercising, sitting still, or
asleep. It only

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.000
records acceleration. To turn that

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.520
signal into something we can interpret,
researchers combine it

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.280
with three things, a documented

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:54.950
processing method, a known wear location
on the body, and a

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.380
defined study protocol.

00:00:56.380 --> 00:01:01.293
Together, those choices turn raw numbers
into outcomes we can

00:01:01.293 --> 00:01:02.340
actually use.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.304
So what does the raw signal actually look
like? It's usually

00:01:05.304 --> 00:01:06.440
stored in gravitational

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:10.112
units written as a lowercase g or in
meters per second

00:01:10.112 --> 00:01:12.560
squared. Further along the pipeline,

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:16.261
we summarize that raw acceleration into
metrics. A common one

00:01:16.261 --> 00:01:18.020
is ENMO, which stands for the

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:21.956
Euclidean Norm Minus One. ENMO subtracts
1g from the signal to

00:01:21.956 --> 00:01:23.480
remove the constant pull

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:28.318
of gravity, leaving behind a clean summary
of dynamic

00:01:28.318 --> 00:01:29.140
movement.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:32.183
This leads to a distinction worth
remembering. Intensity

00:01:32.183 --> 00:01:34.140
summaries, like moderate-to-vigorous

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:38.289
physical activity, often shortened to
MVPA, are not direct

00:01:38.289 --> 00:01:40.220
sensor readings. The device

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:44.439
never measures MVPA. These outcomes are
produced only after we

00:01:44.439 --> 00:01:46.480
apply thresholds or algorithms

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:50.253
to the processed data. Put simply, the raw
signal is the

00:01:50.253 --> 00:01:52.140
evidence, and the outcome is

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:56.033
an interpretation built on top of it. How
does a raw signal

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:57.880
become a defensible research

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:02.558
result through a documented pipeline?
Across this course,

00:02:02.558 --> 00:02:05.020
we'll move through six stages.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:09.407
Plan and deploy, download, organize and
convert, process,

00:02:09.407 --> 00:02:12.100
inspect quality, and finally, clean

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:17.103
and analyze. Lesson 1.1 is the foundation.
Once you understand

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:19.040
what the device records,

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:23.097
every later step has a clear purpose.
Let's recap. An

00:02:23.097 --> 00:02:25.700
accelerometer records acceleration

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:29.593
over time, usually along three axes. It
does not interpret

00:02:29.593 --> 00:02:31.540
behavior on its own. Outcomes

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:35.133
come from combining the signal with a
processing method, a

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:37.240
wear location, and a protocol. And

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:41.183
summaries like ENMO and MVPA are derived,
not directly

00:02:41.183 --> 00:02:41.840
measured.
